Test for Sr.DevOps Engineer
As a senior DevOps engineer, a lot of skills and experience are required. Here in this
test we mainly focus on the following three areas:
Infrastructure
Kubernetes/Container
Pipeline/Automation
But there're definitely more to this role, be prepared for the challenge!
Note, we do things as code, please track progress properly in git with commits and
commit messages.
Task 0: Project Codebase
Pick an open-source project of your choice with multi-tier architecture.
Alternatively, create or imagine a hello-world project yourself with multi-tier
architecture.
Task 1: Infrastructure as Code
Tech Stack (Required): Terraform and its ecosystem.
Cloud Providers (Preferred): Alicloud and/or AWS.
Provision the infrastructure for the project outlined in Task 0, it should include the
following items, (and everything else needed):
Networking (optional, assuming it's already in place)
VPC
Load Balancer
Computing (optional, assuming it's already in place)
Kubernetes
Data Store, one or more of
Relational Database
NoSQL
Redis
S3/OSS
Container Registry (optional, if using public registry)
The project will be deployed to 5 environments: dev, test, perf, staging and
production.
Dev and test are used by development and internal QA testing respectively; Perf is
used for performance testing; Staging can be used for integration with
internal/external teams and UAT.
Optional, for perf, staging and production, this should be a multi-region deployment.
Optional, multi cloud can be used in different environments or regions. This is for
better disaster recovery and also to showcase knowledge on multiple cloud providers.
Task 2: Kubernetes
For the project outlined in Task 0, prepare related kubernets manifests to deploy
them, inlcudes at least
Deployments
Service
Ingress
And includes one or more of the following if appropriate
HPA
cert-manager
Feel free to include anything needed to make life with kubernetes easier.
Note that the same set of services needs to be deployed into multiple environments
(dev, test, perf, staging and production).
Task 3: Pipeline as Code
Tech Stack (Preferred): Harness CI/CD.
Tech Stack (Accepted): All other CI/CD platforms/solutions are accepted as well.
Task 3.1: Optional, Infra Pipeline
For infra outlined in Task 1, prepare a pipeline to deploy the infra. Split the pipeline
into multiple stages/steps, for example, one stage/step for test/plan/approval/apply.
Task 3.2: Required, Service Pipeline
For the project outlined in Task 0, prepare a CI/CD pipeline to build the image(s), and
deploy them to the environment provisioned in Task 1 and Task 2.
Optional, for image build, integrate code quality scan, security scan, unit test, e2e
test, etc. where appropriate;
Optional, for deployment, integrate strategy like blue/green deployment, or canary
deployment, and auto rollback where appropriate.
Task 4: Documentation as Code
For each and every project, we need documentation to pass on the knowledge and
give others high-level overview of the project and design. So please prepare the
following documents/diagrams:
Application design/diagram for the project;
Infrastructure design/diagram for the project;
Pipeline design/diagram for the project.
Tips: For platforms that have visualization of the infra/pipeline/etc. on its platform,
that can be used as well.
Deliverables
Required: For code, deliver all tasks with one or more git repos, either as public
repo(s) on the Internet, or as git archive(s); and send the links/attachments over
email.
Optional: For service deployed, share the public link, or share screenshots.
Optional: For Terraform, if Terraform Cloud is used, share access to the
organization in Terraform Cloud, or share screenshots.
Optional: For pipelines, share access to the platform, or share screenshots.
Notes
The test should be done within one week upon receipt.
If you have limited time for the test, do the tasks that can best showcase your skills.
Don't hesitate to reach out to me if you have any doubts on the test requirements.